//? Title: Ternary search: actual sampled brackets and explicit termination
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Under strict unimodality, comparing two trisection samples discards an outer
third while retaining the extremum. Actual sampled brackets replace the old
report-side replay and separate mathematical contraction from representable
progress.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For a maximum compare f(m1)>=f(m2); keep[lo,m2] when true, otherwise[m1,hi]. For
a minimum reverse the comparison. Ties keep the left interval. Exact arithmetic
width contracts by2/3 per step, giving w_k=w_0*(2/3)^k. This relies on strict
unimodality (with monotone endpoint-extremum cases); arbitrary multimodal
functions and broad flat shoulders have no bracket guarantee. Finite arithmetic
can exhaust strict interior points before tolerance, which is reported
separately. Iteration caps are explicit unresolved stopping controls, not
tolerance certificates.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ternary_search_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/ternary_search.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::TernaryOptions o;
    o.max_iterations = 4;
    auto r = a::ternary_search_max_trace([](double x) {
        return -(x - 1) * (x - 1);
    }, -2, 4, o);
    std::print("| actual bracket before | m1 | m2 | f1 | f2 | keep left | bracket after |\n| --- | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| [{:.6g},{:.6g}] | {:.6g} | {:.6g} | {:.6g} | {:.6g} | {} | [{:.6g},{:.6g}] |\n",
                   s.lo_before, s.hi_before, s.first, s.second, s.first_value,
                   s.second_value, s.kept_left, s.lo_after, s.hi_after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual concave quadratic on[-2,4]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual bracket reductions",
                                     r.result.iterations));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual remaining bracket[{:.3g},{:.3g}]",
                                     r.lo, r.hi));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/ternary_search_tiny.svg");
}
```
